{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.BraidKnot.HeckeAdditiveJucysMurphy","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.HeckeAdditiveJucysMurphy","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:QOU.BraidKnot.HeckeJucysMurphyAdjacentNormalForm"],"declarations":8,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.Hecke.addJM_sigma_prod_swap","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.Hecke.addJM_sigma_prod_swap","kind":"theorem","line":123,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/HeckeAdditiveJucysMurphy.lean#L123-L153","doc":"**The product half only swaps.**  `σ_k (A_k A_{k+1}) = (A_{k+1} A_k) σ_k`.\n\nMathas 3.24(iii) asserts `T_i` commutes with `L_i L_{i+1}` outright and derives commutativity from\nit.  From the **recursion alone** one gets only this swapped form, which is commutation exactly\nwhen `A_k` and `A_{k+1}` already commute — so (iii)'s product half and (iv) are entangled.\n\n**The obstruction survives the change of convention**: this is the same swap seen on the\nmultiplicative side (`sigma_mul_jm_prod`).  Closing it needs the explicit sum-of-transpositions\nexpansion of `L_k`, which an abstract presentation does not provide. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.Hecke.addJM_sigma_comm_add","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.Hecke.addJM_sigma_comm_add","kind":"theorem","line":112,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/HeckeAdditiveJucysMurphy.lean#L112-L121","doc":"**`σ_k` commutes with `A_k + A_{k+1}`, for every `d`.**\n\nThe two exchange relations differ only in swapping `A_k σ_k` for `σ_k A_k`, so those terms cancel\nin the sum.  This is the sum half of Mathas 3.24(iii), and it holds with **no** constraint on the\nnormalisation `d` — cleaner than the multiplicative analogue `sigma_comm_add`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.Hecke.addJM_sigma_right","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.Hecke.addJM_sigma_right","kind":"theorem","line":97,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/HeckeAdditiveJucysMurphy.lean#L97-L110","doc":"**Exchange relation, right**: `A_{k+1} σ_k = h·A_{k+1} + σ_k A_k + d`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.Hecke.addJM_sigma_left","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.Hecke.addJM_sigma_left","kind":"theorem","line":82,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/HeckeAdditiveJucysMurphy.lean#L82-L95","doc":"**Exchange relation, left**: `σ_k A_{k+1} = h·A_{k+1} + A_k σ_k + d`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.Hecke.hecke_smul","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.Hecke.hecke_smul","kind":"theorem","line":77,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/HeckeAdditiveJucysMurphy.lean#L77-L80","doc":"The Hecke relation in scalar-action form. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.Hecke.addJM_succ","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.Hecke.addJM_succ","kind":"theorem","line":74,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/HeckeAdditiveJucysMurphy.lean#L74-L75","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.Hecke.addJM_zero","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.Hecke.addJM_zero","kind":"theorem","line":72,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/HeckeAdditiveJucysMurphy.lean#L72-L72","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.Hecke.addJM","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.Hecke.addJM","kind":"def","line":63,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/HeckeAdditiveJucysMurphy.lean#L63-L70","doc":"**Additive Jucys–Murphy family**, by Mathas's recursion in this corpus's convention:\n`A₀ = 0`, `A_{k+1} = σ_k A_k σ_k + d·σ_k`.\n\nThe scalar `d` is left **free**: every result below holds for all `d`, which is stronger than\nfixing Mathas's `q⁻¹` and makes clear that the sum-commutation owes nothing to the normalisation. ","signatureChunk":0}]}